    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "High blood pressure is a common condition where your heart works too hard to push blood through your body. Taking medicine daily helps keep your heart healthy and stops your blood pressure from getting too high. Eating less salt is very important because salt makes your body hold onto water, which pushes harder on your blood vessels. Light exercise like walking helps your heart work better and keeps your blood pressure low.\n\nYou can do this by walking for a few minutes every day or doing simple stretches. These small changes help your body feel better and stay strong. Always talk to your doctor if you have questions about your medicine or diet. This simple plan protects your heart and keeps you feeling good every day.\n\nTo check your blood pressure at home, buy a special watch or a small box that measures your heart beat. Put the watch on your arm or the box on your wrist before you sleep. Write down the numbers you see on the screen every morning and evening. This helps your doctor know how your body feels and if your medicine is working well.",
